atjaną (whence High German hetzen), but the phonetics are highly problematic. Therefore the group is usually considered imitative, immediately comparable to English hiss.\nThe use for “hoisting” appears first in the mid-15th century in Middle Dutch hîsen (cf. modern Dutch hijsen) and in the Middle English nautical interjection hissa (cf. Scots heeze, English hoise, whence hoist). The word then quickly spread to other Germanic as well as Romance languages. Such cognates include Danish hejse, French hisser, Spanish izar, Italian issare.",null,"haben"]],"senses":[[42372,"hissen","verb","to hoist (a flag or sail)",0,null,null,null,"transitive"]]},"hohlraumes":{"entries":[["hohlraumes",null,null,null]],"senses":[[191685,"hohlraumes","noun","genitive singular of Hohlraum",0]],"inflections":[["hohlraumes","hohlraum","genitive"]]},"knallroter":{"entries":[["knallroter",null,null,null]],"senses":[[506292,"knallroter","adj","inflection of knallrot:",0],[506293,"knallroter","adj","strong/mixed nominative masculine singular",1],[506294,"knallroter","adj","strong genitive/dative feminine singular",2],[506295,"knallroter","adj","strong genitive plural",3]],"inflections":[["knallroter","knallrot","masculine,nominative,singular,strong"]]},"kometenhaftestes":{"entries":[["kometenhaftestes",null,null,null]],"senses":[[508354,"kometenhaftestes","adj","strong/mixed nominative/accusative neuter singular superlative degree of kometenhaft",0]],"inflections":[["kometenhaftestes","kometenhaft","neuter,nominative,singular,strong,superlative,without-article"]]},"mittelwörtern":{"entries":[["mittelwörtern",null,null,null]],"senses":[[607070,"mittelwörtern","noun","dative plural of Mittelwort",0]],"inflections":[["mittelwörtern","mittelwort","dative,definite,plural"]]},"postapokalyptisches":{"entries":[["postapokalyptisches",null,null,null]],"senses":[[533447,"postapokalyptisches","adj","strong/mixed nominative/accusative neuter singular of postapokalyptisch",0]],"inflections":[["postapokalypti